1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
(Episode 4)

2
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:02,140
We have an emergency.

3
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,020
Kataoka was taken.

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,420
I'm afraid VOID is behind this.

5
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,009
Did you sell him out?

6
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:15,066
- What are you talking about?
- I'm talking about Kataoka-san.

7
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:16,090
What are you doing?

8
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:21,270
- Odajima-san!
- Let me go!

9
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,080
- Hey! Get back here!
- Stop!

10
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:24,540
Hey!

11
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:28,220
Stop right there!

12
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,210
- Hey!
- Don't move!

13
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:45,940
Let me go!

14
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:52,510
He really is a fascinating guy.

15
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,220
Anyone who meets young
Kataoka can't help falling for him.

16
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,040
Yes.

17
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,540
If anything goes south,
contact Kumakura-san.

18
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:09,020
Odajima-san.

19
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,790
Since you want to see him
so badly, I'll grant your wish.

20
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:36,970
This is bad.

21
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:09,580
Kataoka-san...

22
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:20,300
In that instant,

23
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:23,240
I knew.

24
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,800
He was someone I must never touch.

25
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:32,760
You get hopelessly drawn to him.

26
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,600
Your eyes just follow
him against your will.

27
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,360
But I can't.

28
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:42,020
I must not touch him.

29
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,400
He is completely...

30
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,300
out of reach.

31
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:21,640
Boss...

32
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,140
What good does it do
if we're both captured?

33
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:43,840
I'm sorry.

34
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,660
To see you,

35
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,600
this was the only way.

36
00:04:56,790 --> 00:05:00,020
Man, you really are something else.

37
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,400
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

38
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,160
Sorry.

39
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,560
They got Odajima-san, too.

40
00:06:20,113 --> 00:06:23,299
Warehouse five in Awakuma City, right?

41
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,500
Yes.

42
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,660
Odajima-san is inside with VOID's guys.

43
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,640
Kataoka-san is probably in there, too.

44
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,740
Let's hope so.

45
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,260
You weren't spotted tailing them, right?

46
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,920
No, sir.

47
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:40,460
I'll scope out the situation inside.

48
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:44,060
Report back the second anything happens.

49
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:46,700
Understood.

50
00:07:07,710 --> 00:07:08,800
Boss.

51
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:12,010
I'm the one who called
Kataoka and Odajima back.

52
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,640
Please, let me go.

53
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:17,280
They've already cut
ties with the Kirii-gumi.

54
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:21,740
Whether civilians live or
die is none of our business.

55
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:23,260
But why would ordinary civilians...

56
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,180
get kidnapped in the first place?

57
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:29,060
There has to be more to this.

58
00:07:50,010 --> 00:07:52,210
They think they're pulling the strings,

59
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:57,140
when they're actually
the ones being played.

60
00:08:09,610 --> 00:08:10,610
Excuse me.

61
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:13,260
I'll take my leave now.

62
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,200
The more clueless they are,

63
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:29,590
the harder they dance
to someone else's tune.

64
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,480
Hey.

65
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,480
That thing's filming us, isn't it?

66
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:44,860
Yeah.

67
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:47,220
Might as well give them a show.

68
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,030
Recklessly chasing after me like that...

69
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,360
Did you miss me that much?

70
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,620
Hello?

71
00:09:00,450 --> 00:09:01,450
Hey!

72
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:07,230
You're so easy to read.

73
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:12,480
Hey, I'm starving over here!

74
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:14,400
Bring us some food! Food!

75
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,080
Or else we're really gonna
start making out right here!

76
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,970
If you don't wanna see
that, bring us some grub!

77
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,940
My grandpa went through hell after the war,

78
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,540
so our family rule is to never
skip three square meals a day!

79
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,650
I know you're listening!

80
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,280
Um, Boss...

81
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:33,880
Huh?

82
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,680
Whoa, hey.

83
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,740
Are those brains of
yours just for decoration?

84
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,070
How are we supposed
to eat tied up like this?

85
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,500
Wait, what about me?

86
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,800
How come only you get untied?

87
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,700
Sorry about that...

88
00:10:46,850 --> 00:10:47,979
Oh, rice balls.

89
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,180
How are you so calm right now?

90
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,120
Sorry.

91
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:55,560
Well, that makes one thing clear.

92
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:59,880
If they're feeding us, they're
not killing us right away.

93
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,530
If they just wanted me dead,

94
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:07,050
they would've just shot me back there.

95
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:13,220
Going to the trouble of kidnapping me and
keeping me alive means there's a reason.

96
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:15,320
Right.

97
00:11:16,590 --> 00:11:17,980
Am I the target?

98
00:11:21,060 --> 00:11:23,030
Anyway, let's just eat first.

99
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:06,570
Plum and tuna mayo.

100
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,810
Which one do you want first?

101
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,070
Tuna mayo, obviously.

102
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:11,310
Okay.

103
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,820
Here you go.

104
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,320
Mmm...

105
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:37,180
Come to think of it,
we've done this before.

106
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:39,020
You feeding me like this.

107
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,160
Yes.

108
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:46,190
Some kid asked me to help, so I
spent all night keeping a baby bird warm.

109
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,450
- I bought some food.
- Oh.

110
00:12:54,770 --> 00:12:57,420
You idiot, how am I supposed to eat ramen?

111
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,710
Didn't you just say
my hands were occupied?

112
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:01,900
I'm sorry.

113
00:13:03,110 --> 00:13:04,360
The rice balls will do.

114
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,700
Hurry up and feed me.

115
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:12,180
I got salmon and tuna mayo.

116
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,720
Tuna mayo, obviously.

117
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:33,180
That's right.

118
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,000
You were so clumsy back
then, you even spilled the ramen.

119
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,880
You remember that really well.

120
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:40,290
Of course I do.

121
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,950
How could I ever forget?

122
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,120
Here you go.

123
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,040
Thanks.

124
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:01,896
You've gotten pretty good at this.

125
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,040
Your feeding skills, I mean.

126
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,009
I can take care of you forever, Boss.

127
00:14:06,010 --> 00:14:07,220
Hey, what is this, elder care?

128
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,500
I'm not that old yet.

129
00:14:09,050 --> 00:14:10,770
I'll take care of you when you're old, too.

130
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:13,220
That almost sounds like a proposal.

131
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,660
Does that mean you're
gonna grow old with me?

132
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,020
Though we're already married anyway.

133
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:29,020
Hmm?

134
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,440
Hmm?

135
00:14:37,370 --> 00:14:38,370
Hmm?

136
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,500
I...

137
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:53,570
have never once thought about...

138
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,350
ever leaving your side.

139
00:15:05,690 --> 00:15:07,540
You're getting cuter by the day.

140
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,530
Odajima.

141
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,470
Um...

142
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:32,720
Hmm?

143
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
The reason you...

144
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,220
married me in the first place...

145
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,920
Now that you mention
it, I still haven't told you.

146
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:46,500
The reason I married you.

147
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:53,000
I'll tell you once we get back.

148
00:15:54,070 --> 00:15:55,070
Ren.

149
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Odajima.

150
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,510
No, not that.

151
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,840
Kiss me.

152
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:19,620
You make the first move for once.

153
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:23,370
Give me a kiss and I'll tell you.

154
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:26,400
Wait...

155
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,200
Um...

156
00:16:33,530 --> 00:16:35,340
Seeing you look so reluctant...

157
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:37,160
is so much fun.

158
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,370
You haven't changed a bit.

159
00:16:42,790 --> 00:16:43,790
Come on.

160
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:51,500
They're watching.

161
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:53,680
Who cares?

162
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:55,360
Let's give them a show.

163
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:57,260
Come here.

164
00:17:20,490 --> 00:17:22,000
You will never...

165
00:17:22,330 --> 00:17:24,250
find happiness.

166
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:29,270
Never...

167
00:17:29,420 --> 00:17:31,840
find happiness.

168
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:34,880
Odajima...

169
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:40,380
I...

170
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,520
can never...

171
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:45,620
be happy...

172
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:49,780
I don't deserve...

173
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:52,220
to be happy...

174
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,760
Consider this a warning.

175
00:18:23,220 --> 00:18:24,740
Stay out of the Kirii-gumi's business.

176
00:18:25,866 --> 00:18:27,466
Do as you're told, and we'll let you go.

177
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:56,320
Kataoka-san! Odajima-san!

178
00:19:00,950 --> 00:19:01,950
Boss...

179
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,430
Please hurry...

180
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,240
Who's behind this?

181
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:07,779
Who's your boss?

182
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,100
We don't take questions.

183
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,870
You don't have a choice.

184
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,480
Please save Kataoka...

185
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:27,120
and Odajima.

186
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:30,060
I told you, I have no
obligation to step in.

187
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,340
But...

188
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,340
Kataoka did this for our family...

189
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,880
I never asked him to.

190
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,690
Calling the two of them back...

191
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:41,640
was my mistake.

192
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:43,340
Even so,

193
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,320
you can't just leave them
to die either, can you, Boss?

194
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:56,020
You made this mess.
Why should I clean it up?

195
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:00,250
Our ties with those two...

196
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,240
run deep.

197
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:06,340
Letting ordinary civilians get killed...

198
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:08,970
would bring shame to our family.

199
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,580
Boss!

200
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:32,560
Excuse me.

201
00:20:49,370 --> 00:20:51,050
Shut your mouth, go back to Okinawa,

202
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:53,580
and stay out of
Kirii-gumi's business, right?

203
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,500
Not that I asked to get dragged into this.

204
00:21:06,510 --> 00:21:07,570
I refuse.

205
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,950
I don't take orders from anyone.

206
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,500
Is this about yakuza pride?

207
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:20,140
Drop the tough guy act.
You're out of the game.

208
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,960
This has nothing to do with being yakuza.

209
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,700
It's about my pride as a man.

210
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:27,380
- Hey, Odajima.
- Yes.

211
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:47,820
What's going on?

212
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,160
I'm sorry!

213
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:50,716
We patted them down thoroughly...

214
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:52,140
Come on, what are you, amateurs?

215
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:54,990
Taking the shoes is Kidnapping 101.

216
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:59,060
You're completely outnumbered.

217
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:01,860
What's one little blade gonna do?

218
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,440
You don't stand a chance.

219
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:07,960
Fair point.

220
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,200
However...

221
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,810
it's plenty to kill just me.

222
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:18,920
What are you doing?

223
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,000
Take us to your boss.

224
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:24,720
If you don't, he'll slit my throat.

225
00:22:26,090 --> 00:22:28,800
If we die, the Kirii-gumi
will be out for blood.

226
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:32,420
And your mastermind's
grand plan goes up in smoke.

227
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:34,740
Right after I kill you, I'll join you.

228
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,280
Good.

229
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,000
That's my wifey.

230
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:41,000
Like you have the guts to do it!

231
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:44,530
Never underestimate

232
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:46,240
the resolve of an ex-yakuza!

233
00:22:57,870 --> 00:22:59,120
That's enough.

234
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:17,960
(Next Episode Preview)

235
00:23:17,961 --> 00:23:20,260
The heads of the Koutokukai and Kirii-gumi.

236
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:24,780
You said tensions are so high that an all-out
war could break out if they meet, right?

237
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:25,900
Damn it.

238
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:30,360
They're no use to us
alive, so let's just kill them.

239
00:23:30,540 --> 00:23:33,620
Come at me, you bastards!

240
00:23:34,370 --> 00:23:36,780
Looks like you guys are having a blast.

241
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:39,040
Die!

242
00:23:40,670 --> 00:23:41,670
It's over.

243
00:23:44,170 --> 00:23:45,420
Kataoka-san!
